          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.088,
            0.771,
            0.11
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Example 5: Construct a triangle with angles in the ratio 1 : 3 : 5."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.113,
            0.846,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": "We know that the sum of the angles in a triangle is 180°. So the angles are C"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.151,
            0.517,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A}=180^{\\circ} \\times \\frac{1}{(1+3+5)}=180^{\\circ} \\times \\frac{1}{9}=20^{\\circ}.",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.181,
            0.517,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{B}=180^{\\circ} \\times \\frac{3}{(1+3+5)}=180^{\\circ} \\times \\frac{3}{9}=60^{\\circ}.",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.209,
            0.524,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": "\\angle C = 180^{\\circ} \\times \\frac{5}{(1 + 3 + 5)} = 180^{\\circ} \\times \\frac{5}{9} = 100^{\\circ}.",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.541,
            0.138,
            0.912,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.241,
            0.294,
            0.264
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.266,
            0.848,
            0.343
          ],
          "content": "1. A cricket coach schedules practice sessions that include different activities in a specific ratio — time for warm-up/cool-down : time for batting : time for bowling : time for fielding : : 3 : 4 : 3 : 5. If each session is 150 minutes long, how much time is spent on each activity?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.351,
            0.847,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "2. A school library has books in different languages in the following ratio no. of Odiya books : no. of Hindi books : no. of English books :: 3 : 2 : 1. If the library has 288 Odiya books, how many Hindi and English books does it have?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.436,
            0.848,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": "3. I have 100 coins in the ratio — no. of ₹10 coins : no. of ₹5 coins : no. of ₹2 coins : no. of ₹1 coins :: 4 : 3 : 2 : 1. How much money do I have in coins?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.502,
            0.801,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "4. Construct a triangle with sidelengths in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. Will all the triangles drawn with this ratio of sidelengths be congruent to each other? Why or why not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.816,
            0.493,
            0.903,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.568,
            0.8,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": "5. Can you construct a triangle with sidelengths in the ratio 1 : 3 : 5? Why or why not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.636,
            0.433,
            0.659
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "3.5 A Slice of the Pie"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.67,
            0.64,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": "Have you seen pie charts like the one shown in the figure? Pie charts show different proportions of a whole. This one shows the proportions of students that have scored each grade in an assessment. These kinds of visualisations help us quickly interpret data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.78,
            0.639,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": "Let us try to create this pie chart. Here is a table showing the grades scored by students:"
        },
